    {
      "sourceField": "monitor",
      "sourceExcerpt": "• Check HR and BP before the dose. • Report symptomatic bradycardia, significant hypotension or new conduction problems. • During heart-failure titration, review new worsening dyspnea or congestion. • Do not abruptly stop chronic therapy without a prescribing plan; withdrawal can cause sympathetic rebound and renewed cardiac symptoms. • Check for duplicate beta-blockade. • Relative beta1 selectivity does not eliminate bronchospasm risk: asthma/bronchospastic disease requires prescriber review rather than assuming respiratory safety.",
